<title>CHINA: China invites tenders for new BOT power plant.</title>
<headline>China invites tenders for new BOT power plant.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has invited international tenders for a new power plant in southern Hunan province to be built under a build-operate-transfer agreement, the Financial News said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The first phase of the new Changsha power station would have two coal-fired generators with a capacity of 350,000 kilowatts each, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The cabinet's State Planning Commission had approved the plant and the Hunan provincial government had invited international tenders for the project, it said but gave no further details.</p>
</text>
